              "body": ":stop_sign: **Crash Risk**: The test binds a `TcpListener` to get a free port (line 157), drops it immediately (line 159), then re-uses that port string to start the gRPC server (line 161). There is a TOCTOU race: another process can bind the same port between `drop(probe)` and `op_grpc_bridge::serve(addr, core)`. The fix is to pass the already-bound `TcpListener` directly into the `serve` function (using `serve_with_incoming` or equivalent) rather than dropping it and re-binding. This pattern is repeated in `client_roundtrip_set_get_subscribe` on lines 300–304 with the same risk.",
